LICENSE AND PROVENANCE
======================

This repository redistributes rebuilt RPM packages of PHP 7.4 for Enterprise Linux 7.
It is an unofficial community rebuild and is not affiliated with or endorsed by the PHP
project, Remi Collet, Red Hat, or any Linux distribution.

Packaged software
-----------------
- PHP itself is distributed under the PHP License, version 3.01.
  See https://www.php.net/license/ for the authoritative text. Individual bundled
  components (Zend Engine, SQLite, etc.) carry their own licenses as stated in the PHP
  source distribution. Each binary RPM declares its license in its own metadata
  (`rpm -qi <package>` shows the `License:` field).

Packaging
---------
- The RPM spec file and all patches — including the php2shell mitigation patch
  (CVE-2026-109618 / CVE-2026-109619) — are the work of Remi Collet and come from his
  `php74` package at https://rpms.remirepo.net/ and https://git.remirepo.net/.
  They retain their upstream licensing. This repository does not relicense them.

This repository's own additions
-------------------------------
- The documentation (README, BUILD notes), the two EL7 build adjustments described in
  BUILD.md, and the repository metadata are released into the public domain (CC0 1.0).
  Do whatever you want with them; no warranty.

NO WARRANTY
-----------
These packages are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. PHP 7.4 and CentOS 7
are end-of-life. Use these packages at your own risk, as a temporary measure while you
plan a migration to a supported platform. Verify the signatures and checksums, and review
the source (the published src.rpm) before trusting anything here on your systems.
